            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0530" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 342.112Sm6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Curtis to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bridgeburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Walter Smith, Buffalo, N. Y., shot and killed; Charles Dorsch, Buffalo, N. Y.,
                    shot through lung by private in Canadian militia in Fort Erie this morning.
                    These men were duck shooting and did not land when ordered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Curtis</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
